<description>
Draw orange corridors along a nearest-visible-block walk from the red 2x2 block through teal 2x2 blocks.

Input structure
- The background contains one red 2x2 start block and multiple teal 2x2 target blocks.
- Blocks may align in shared two-row or two-column bands; non-background pixels between aligned blocks block visibility.

Rule
- Start at the red block.
- Among unvisited teal blocks visible in the same horizontal or vertical band, choose the unique nearest one.
- Paint the background gap between the current block and that teal block orange, then continue from that teal block.
- Stop when no unvisited teal block is visible from the current block.

Key insight
- The output is not the full alignment graph; it is a greedy nearest-neighbor walk whose line of sight is blocked by any existing colored block.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "red 2x2 start object",
  "path": "greedy walk from the current object to the unique nearest unvisited teal 2x2 object visible in the same two-row or two-column band; visibility requires the gap between objects to be background, and the walk stops when no such teal object exists",
  "trajectory": "paint the 2-pixel-wide background gap between consecutive objects orange",
  "transform": "preserve all red and teal objects; leave teal objects not reached by the walk unchanged",
  "multi_step": "after each connection, the reached teal object becomes the current object; already visited objects are not chosen again"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 16-26 rows x 18-28 cols, black (0) background
  blocks:
    shape: all blocks are exactly 2x2
    colors: 1 red (2) start block + 2-11 teal (8) target blocks
    placement: no block touches grid edge; min gap between any two block bboxes >= 1 cell
  walk:
    rule: greedy nearest-visible-neighbor from red through teal blocks
    visibility: two blocks are visible iff they share exact row-band or col-band (both top/bottom rows or both left/right cols match) and the 2-wide corridor between them is all background
    selection: at each step, among visible unvisited teal blocks, the nearest (by row or col offset) must be unique
    length: 1-9 steps with 0-6 direction changes (turns between h/v)
    gap_distance: 1-10 cells between consecutive blocks on the walk (block center offset minus 2)
  unvisited_teal: 0-4 teal blocks not reached by the walk; these are not aligned with the walk endpoint or are blocked [observed]
  output:
    same as input plus orange (7) pixels filling the 2-wide corridor between each consecutive pair on the walk
    all original red and teal blocks preserved unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: path-first
